**V5 closes five of the six round-four gaps. Replacement timing is still open, and the new split rule can change what counts as a decided answer.** For example, if one reader says “unsupported” and the other says “insufficient,” forcing a decided mark in both counts can add an answer that D428 says to leave out. [V5 split rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v5.md:136) · [D428](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4761)

- **Replacement draws — partly resolved.** V5 fixes eligibility, the one-per-system limit, and the $360 maximum. The same historical article window does not satisfy D431’s same-day send requirement. Keep a later replacement diagnostic, or explicitly supersede the timing rule before launch. The recorded spend decision should cover replacements as well as the original six draws. [Replacement rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v5.md:153) · [Spend decision](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v5.md:231) · [D431](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/DECISIONS-log.md:4795) · [Same-day definition](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/WIRING-DESIGN.md:7)
- **Guardrail minimum — resolved.** Only unsplit decided cards count toward ten. **New gap:** for the rates themselves, specify how each count handles a split with an insufficient mark. If that count selects insufficient, leave it out of the decided denominator. [V5 guardrails](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v5.md:136)
- **Duplicates and direction — both resolved.** Distinct bets count toward 30 in both readings. The earlier opening is the original, and the later duplicate stays in the worth guardrail. [V5 identity rule](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v5.md:118)
- **Unmeasured Step 2 checks — resolved.** An undersized check cannot clear release. **Census roots — resolved.** Both the main checkout and worktrees include tests, mock data, and UI fixtures. [Step 2 checks](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v5.md:200) · [Census scope](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-17-product-comparison/RUN-PLAN-v5.md:50)

**NOT READY: settle replacement timing under D431 and freeze how a split with an insufficient mark enters each guardrail count.**
